# SHA-256 digests of the `freeze` release archives screenshots/install-freeze.sh
# installs, copied verbatim from the release's own checksums.txt. Pinned HERE so
# the trust root is this repository rather than the download's origin.
#
# `freeze_version` in that script is the only place the version is decided; these
# lines are upstream's data for it, and the script refuses to install when it
# finds no line for the archive that version names, which is what makes a bump
# that forgets to refresh this file fail rather than install something unchecked.
# Refresh from the release's own checksums.txt under
# https://github.com/charmbracelet/freeze/releases/.
ba1164c2e6d573af32df13ddc5868f7cdfc8b9992f26f53695787ca5f4274023  freeze_0.2.2_Linux_arm64.tar.gz
012fdbdd16c0c19570f9052aac34d16d93d7d0d3b565b05374cc59492f53539b  freeze_0.2.2_Linux_x86_64.tar.gz
